TEXT 64 -128 Left 3 ;LMG1210 + 2x parallel EPC2361 per switch: separate DC-link, power loops and gate loops
TEXT 64 -80 Left 2 ;One LMG1210 drives both legs. Each EPC2361 has its own RGON/RGOFF, ON/OFF diodes and gate-loop inductance.
TEXT 64 -32 Left 2 ;Each leg n has its own CDCn + LCAPn (ESL) and LPOWERn commutation loop; legs share BUS/PGND through LFEED per leg.
TEXT 64 16 Left 2 ;SW and low-side source (0) are common ideal nodes: ideal Kelvin returns, no common-source or inter-device source inductance.
TEXT 1704 80 Left 2 ;QH1 gate (HO -> GH1, return SW)
TEXT 2272 88 Left 2 ;QH2 gate (HO -> GH2, return SW)
TEXT 2912 128 Left 2 ;QL1 gate (LO -> GL1, return 0)
TEXT 3488 128 Left 2 ;QL2 gate (LO -> GL2, return 0)
TEXT 1440 1008 Left 2 ;LEG 1: loop 1 = LPOWER1 + LCAP1
TEXT 1440 1712 Left 2 ;LEG 2: loop 2 = LPOWER2 + LCAP2
TEXT 64 832 Left 2 !.include LMG1210_modes.lib
TEXT 64 864 Left 2 !.include EPC2361.lib
TEXT 64 896 Left 2 !.param FSW=100k DUTY=0.9 DEAD=50n TR=2n TS=20u T=1/FSW
TEXT 64 928 Left 2 !.model DBOOT D(Is=1n N=1.2 Rs=1 Cjo=2p Tt=1n Bv=150 Ibv=10u)
TEXT 64 960 Left 2 !.model DGATE D(Is=1u N=1.05 Rs=0.05 Cjo=5p Tt=0 Bv=30)
TEXT 64 992 Left 2 !.tran 0 {TSTOP} 0 5n
TEXT 64 1024 Left 2 !.param TSTOP=5m
TEXT 64 1088 Left 2 !.param RGON_H1=10 RGOFF_H1=2 LGATE_H1=10n
TEXT 64 1120 Left 2 !.param RGON_H2=10 RGOFF_H2=2 LGATE_H2=10n
TEXT 64 1152 Left 2 !.param RGON_L1=6 RGOFF_L1=6 LGATE_L1=30n
TEXT 64 1184 Left 2 !.param RGON_L2=6 RGOFF_L2=6 LGATE_L2=30n
TEXT 64 1248 Left 2 !.param CDC1=10u LPOWER1=2n LCAP1=0.5n
TEXT 64 1280 Left 2 !.param CDC2=10u LPOWER2=2.5n LCAP2=0.5n
TEXT 64 1312 Left 2 !.param LFEED=5n
TEXT 64 1376 Left 2 ;DUTY = requested high-side fraction before dead-time subtraction (0 < DUTY < 1).
TEXT 64 1408 Left 2 ;Require min(DUTY,1-DUTY)/FSW > DEAD+TR. Bootstrap requires low-side charging time.
TEXT 64 1440 Left 2 ;Skew per-device RG/LGATE or per-leg LPOWER/LCAP/CDC to study current sharing.
TEXT 64 1472 Left 2 ;LFEED = total BUS->leg + leg->PGND interconnect per leg (decouples the two DC links).
TEXT 64 1504 Left 2 ;Compare I(LPPLUS1) vs I(LPPLUS2), V(GH1,SW) vs V(GH2,SW), V(GL1) vs V(GL2).
